---
description: "State management, API typing, and view states (frontend/)."
globs: "frontend/src/features/**/*.ts,frontend/src/features/**/*.tsx,frontend/src/features/**/*.js,frontend/src/features/**/*.jsx,frontend/src/lib/**/*.ts,frontend/src/lib/**/*.tsx,frontend/src/lib/**/*.js,frontend/src/lib/**/*.jsx,frontend/src/pages/**/*.ts,frontend/src/pages/**/*.tsx,frontend/src/pages/**/*.js,frontend/src/pages/**/*.jsx"
alwaysApply: false
---

State + data rules:
- Prefer local state (useState) for UI state.
- For shared state across many components:
  - Ask before introducing Zustand or any external store.
  - If user approves, keep store minimal and typed.
- API calls must go through a typed client in `frontend/src/lib/apiClient.ts`.
- All API payloads/responses must have TypeScript types in `frontend/src/types/`.

Loading/empty/error:
- Every data-driven screen must have loading, empty, and error states.
- Prefer skeletons for loading lists/cards.

Formatting:
- Use shared utilities for date/currency display in `frontend/src/lib/format.ts`.
- Do not do money math with floats; treat numbers as display only and rely on backend for calculations.
